0..68 Comment "/// This source compares one lambda with a composite of two lambdas."
69..72 Comment "///"
73..138 Comment "/// The two lambda bodies return the same path for each argument."
139..194 Comment "/// A bind over the inner composite reads its endpoint."
195..275 Comment "/// A transport that sticks on `g` returns the value that it moves, at any path."
276..336 Comment "/// So the bind is the transport along `h` at that endpoint."
337..340 Comment "///"
341..411 Comment "/// The kernel evaluates the composite calls inside the action motive."
412..466 Comment "/// The two codes then compare by the same path rules."
467..470 Comment "///"
471..515 Comment "/// - see: #3824 — returning variable call"
516..553 Comment "/// - see: #4011 — lambda composite"
554..591 Comment "/// - see: #4005 — composite action"
593..646 Comment "/// The `composeAfter` function composes `F` and `G`."
